Z||000000||fotofrank||02-28-2001||01:02 PM|||| The car is a 1984 SE, Duke engine. It has a Holly tbi and intake, an MSD coil and an MSD 6A. the car started and ran fine till a new started(old one had heat soak problem). Now the car will not starty. Gas is getting to the TBI and the spark is a strong blue. Engine turns over but no go. Wires,plugs distributor cap and rotor replaced. Now what?<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-28-2001||01:52 PM||||Same thing happened on Jaygee79's Fiero. I couldn't figure it out. It ended up being the fusible link. It looked fine but was corroded on the inside. I cut it out and replaced it with an inline fuse and it started right up. It was in the wire harness that ran close to the belt. I think the wires run over to the alt. and around the front of the engine. The fusible link was up near the Batt. end of those wires.<P>I just helped Fiero 5 with the same thing too.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||02-28-2001||10:21 PM||||  Found the problem with no start. The o2 sensor is bad. Installed a new one and it started right up. Now it seems my CAT is clogged. car only does 15MPH.                  Thanks for your input TheFiero64<BR><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||9
